  - "cargo xtask verify-doc — 40 docs checked, none red (the three new designs green as component-design, the WU plan green as wu-plan)."
  - "cargo xtask ui specimens --check — all three design files render over file:// in headless Chrome with zero console errors; every spec-* mount fills (field 3 buttons, status-dot 13, disclosure 1 mount)."
  - "cargo xtask gate0 — fmt + clippy -D warnings + all tests green (107 passed)."
standalone_commit:
  sha: e71987c
  what: "doc-assets/components/tw-config.js — a stale ../../../ import that has resolved outside the repo since the E-DFLOW.W5 asset move."
  level: commit
  waived: "A build-asset path fix with no product surface and no runtime reachable from a test: the file is loaded only by a browser opening a design doc over file://, where the failure mode is a silently unthemed page rather than an error any suite can observe."
  evidence: "Direct resolution check, before and after — `node --input-type=module -e \"import('./doc-assets/components/tw-config.js')\"` failed with `Cannot find module '/Users/.../proj/misc/ui/tailwind.config.js'` (note the path escaping the repo root) and after the fix resolves, reaching the expected `tailwind is not defined` (that global exists only in a browser with the Play CDN loaded). Path arithmetic confirmed independently: doc-assets/components/ → ui/ is two levels, not three."
note: "The three design files in this WU do NOT exercise this fix — they load specimens.bundle.js, which inlines its own theme block with its own correct path, so the render gate above passes either way. An earlier draft of this note claimed the gate covered it; that was wrong and is corrected here. The files that still load tw-config.js through a live script tag are exactly two, both outside this diff: docs/design-flow.html:8 and docs/component-design.html:8 (docs/decisions/dec-26-the-mockup-mounts.html names the file in prose only, and an earlier draft of this note wrongly counted it as a loader) — which is precisely why the bug survived: nothing that runs in CI opens them."
